{title: Fruit That Will Last}
{subtitle: John 15:16}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 76}
{time: 2/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] | [Eb] | [Eb] | [Bb] |
| [Bb] | [Cm7] | [Cm7] | [Ab] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
You did not pick [Eb]me out of the [Bb]crowd
I chose no [Cm7]one, I was [Ab]found
Your voice reached [Eb]out to lift me up
[Bb]A new and quiet [Cm7]purpose in my cup [Ab]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Eb]Go and bear [Bb]fruit that will [Cm7]last
A [Eb]harvest built to [Bb]stand the [Cm7]blast
Ask the Fa[Abmaj7]ther in my [Bb]name
He will [Cm7]give, He will [Abmaj7]not shame
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
No longer [Eb]servants in the [Bb]dark
Knowing the [Cm7]master is far from the [Ab]mark
I have told [Eb]you what I heard from Him
[Bb]A friendship [Cm7]deep, and close, and [Ab]dim
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Love one an[Bb]other is [Cm7]the command
In this [Abmaj7]world, [Bb]hand in [Cm7]hand
If they [Abmaj7]hate you, they [Bb]hated me [Cm7]first
Out of the [Abmaj7]world, you have been [Bb]placed
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Eb]Go and bear [Bb]fruit that will [Cm]last
A [Eb]harvest built to [Bb]stand the [Cm7]blast
Ask the Fa[Abmaj7]ther in my [Bb]name
He will [Cm7]give, He will [Abmaj7]not shame
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
I [Eb]chose you out of the [Bb]world
Your fruit will [Cm7]last, it is un[Abmaj7]furled
{end_of_verse}
